            "Suitable for": "Have oily and acne-prone skin? This face wash is for you!\n\nThis face wash is great for people with combination skin",
            "Patch testing": "We at The Derma Co. take skincare seriously. To us, solving problems remains the primary goal. We want to ensure each one of you that our products are dermatologist-approved and highly effective.\n\nSteps for Patch Testing:-\n\n1. Clean a patch of skin on the upper forearm and apply a small amount of the product\n\n2. Wait for 15-20 minutes or a maximum of 30 minutes\n\n3. If any itching, redness, burning, blistering or irritation is observed, wash the area, and do not use the product\n\nPlease Note: A patch test is only for determining early irritation reaction to product(s) and does not promise similar results when applied to other areas(s) of the body, including the face or after regular use. A patch test does not account for any underlying conditions and should not be used for the diagnosis of hypersensitivity or allergic contact dermatitis.",
            "Ingredients List": "Aqua, Cocamidopropyl Betaine, Cocamidopropyl Hydroxysultaine, Maltooligosyl Glucoside and Hydrogenated Starch Hydrolysate, Decyl Glucoside, Disodium Laureth Sulfosuccinate, Sodium Lauroyl Sarcosinate, Propylene Glycol, Glycerin, Salicylic Acid, Zinc PCA, Allantoin, Sodium Cocoyl Isethionate, Coco-Glucoside & Glyceryl Oleate, Glucono Delta Lactone, Capryloyl Glycine & Sarcosine & Cinnamomum Zeylanicum Bark Extract, DMDM Hydantoin & Methylchloroisothiazolinone & Methylisothiazolinone, Sodium Hydroxide.",
            "FAQ": "Can I Use this Derma Co Salicylic Acid Foaming Face Wash Every Day?\n\nYes, you can use this face wash every day. For best results, use twice a day.\n\nAre There Any Side Effects I Should Be Worried About?\n\nNo. There are no side effects of using 1% Salicylic Acid Foaming Daily Face Wash. However, a patch test is recommended before using the product.\n\nIs this Derma Co Salicylic Acid Foaming Face Wash Suitable For Oily Skin?\n\nYes, the Salicylic Acid in the face wash targets acne by penetrating deep into the skin while reducing the oil production.\n\nHow do you use derma co-salicylic foaming face wash?\n\nIncorporating The Derma Co Salicylic Acid Foaming Face Wash is simpler. Usually, washing your face & skin is the first step in your skincare routine. First, dampen your skin and pump out an adequate amount of The Derma Co Salicylic face wash on your hands. Next, gently massage it over the wet skin in a circular motion. Lastly, rinse well and pat dry. Follow it up with a matching moisturizer as per your skin type for the best results.\n\nCan I use derma co salicylic acid Facewash daily?\n\nYes, you can use The Derma Co 1% Salicylic Acid Face Wash every day. The derma co 1 salicylic acid gel face wash ingredients such as Salicylic Acid and Zinc PCA & PHA, which are safe for all skin types. Salicylic Acid penetrates the skin and helps dissolve the unwanted debris clogged in the skin pores. This helps eliminate various signs of premature aging, such as acne, blackheads, and whiteheads. The Salicylic Acid face wash for oily skin contains Zinc PCA is an anti-microbial agent which helps regulate oil production and acne-causing bacteria. It also has PHA, which is a gentle yet effective exfoliator that helps remove dead skin cells, giving your skin a smoother and brighter skin.\n\nCan I leave the derma co 1% salicylic acid foaming daily face wash overnight?\n\nA good-quality face wash with salicylic acid is designed to remove impurities, germs, dirt, and makeup that can irritate the skin. Therefore, when left on the skin for a long time or overnight, it may strip off your skin's natural moisture and oils. We thus advise avoiding leaving The Derma Co Salicylic Acid Face Wash on your face overnight. You should rather apply a moisturizer (after you have washed your face with the face wash) and leave it applied overnight.\n\nWhat is the best age to start using Salicylic Acid?\n\nExperts recommend one should start using Salicylic-based skincare products over the age of 18-20 years. Before using Salicylic Acid-based skincare products such as salicylic acid face wash, you should always perform a patch test at least 48 hours before using salicylic acid products. If you experience any discomfort, you should consult your skincare experts.\n\nIs Salicylic Acid Face Wash good for the face?\n\nYes, The Salicylic Acid Face Wash is good for the face. It helps target acne by penetrating deep into the skin and reduces the amount of excess oil produced in the skin by the activity of oil glands. The Derma Salicylic Acid Face Wash also helps clear out clogged skin pores, which can aggravate acne and other skin concerns. It is non-comedogenic and is suitable for all skin types.",
            "Disclaimer And Additional Information": "1. The product contains natural ingredients & may change color and fragrance, without losing effectiveness.\n\n2. Even natural ingredients can cause and trigger existing allergies. A patch test is recommended.\n\n3. In case of any rashes or allergy, please consult a specialist.\n\n4. All images shown are for illustration purpose only, actual results may vary.\n\n5. For external use only. Store in a cool & dry place.",
