            "Patch testing": "We at The Derma Co. take skincare seriously. To us, solving problems remains the primary goal. We want to ensure each one of you that our products are dermatologist-approved and highly effective.\n\nSteps for Patch Testing:-\n\n1. Clean a patch of skin on the upper forearm and apply a small amount of the product\n\n2. Wait for 15-20 minutes or a maximum of 30 minutes\n\n3. If any itching, redness, burning, blistering or irritation is observed, wash the area, and do not use the product\n\nPlease Note: A patch test is only for determining early irritation reaction to product(s) and does not promise similar results when applied to other areas(s) of the body, including the face or after regular use. A patch test does not account for any underlying conditions and should not be used for the diagnosis of hypersensitivity or allergic contact dermatitis.",
            "Ingredients List": "Aqua, Sodium Alpha Olefin Sulfonate, Cocamidopropyl Betaine, Glycerin, Cocamide MEA, Sodium Lactate, Salicylic Acid, Salix Alba (Willow) Bark Extract, Hamamelis Virginiana (Witch Hazel) Extract, Coco-Glucoside,Glyceryl Oleate, PEG-120 Methyl Glucose Dioleate, Sodium Chloride, Phenoxyethanol, Triethylene glycol & Disodium EDTA.",
            "FAQ": "Is Derma Co Salicylic Acid Gel Face Wash good for your face?\n\nYes, The Derma Co 1% Salicylic Acid Gel Face Wash is a dermatologically tested formula designed to deep cleanse pores and control oil while being gentle on the skin. It is safe and effective for daily use on acne-prone skin.\n\nCan I apply Derma Co Salicylic Acid Gel Face Wash daily?\n\nYes, this salicylic acid face wash for oily skin can be used twice daily to control excess oil and prevent pimples without over-drying.\n\nDoes Derma Co Salicylic Acid Gel Face Wash remove tan?\n\nIt helps clear dead skin cells and dirt, improving radiance over time, but it is not formulated as a tan-removal product.\n\nIs Derma Co Salicylic Acid Gel Face Wash good for oily skin?\n\nYes. This face wash with salicylic acid is perfect for oily and acne-prone skin, helping regulate sebum and reduce clogged pores.\n\nWhat are the benefits of using Salicylic Acid Gel Face Wash?\n\nKey salicylic acid face wash benefits include exfoliation, oil control, and clearer-looking skin by reducing acne-causing impurities.\n\nWhat is the Derma Co 1% Salicylic Acid Gel for oily skin and acne with Witch Hazel?\n\nIt is a gentle cleanser that contains 1% Salicylic Acid (for exfoliation and sebum regulation) and Witch Hazel (astringent) to deeply clean pores and calm active acne.\n\nHow do you use The Derma Co Salicylic Acid Gel Face Wash?\n\nApply a small amount to wet skin, massage gently for a few seconds, and rinse thoroughly. Use twice daily.\n\nWhat is 1% Salicylic Acid Gel Daily Face Wash used for?\n\nIt is used to exfoliate, unclog pores, and reduce acne and blackheads while keeping the skin fresh and oil-free.\n\nWhich skin type is The Derma Co Salicylic Acid Face Wash good for?\n\nIt is best for oily and acne-prone skin but also suitable for combination types. Those with dry skin should use it sparingly.\n\nWhat are the ingredients in a Salicylic Acid Gel Face Wash?\n\nKey ingredients include 1% Salicylic Acid, Willow Bark, and Witch Hazel.\n\nAre there any side effects of using Derma Co Salicylic Acid Face Wash?\n\nIt is generally safe but can cause mild dryness in very sensitive skin. Always patch test before use.\n\nIs The Derma Co Salicylic Acid Gel Face Wash non-comedogenic?\n\nYes, it is a non-comedogenic salicylic acid face wash that cleanses pores without clogging them.\n\nWhat is the best salicylic acid face wash dermatologist recommended in India?\n\nThe Derma Co 1% Salicylic Acid Gel Face Wash is among the best salicylic acid face washes that are dermatologist recommended in India for acne-prone skin.",
            "Disclaimer And Additional Information": "1. The product contains natural ingredients & may change color and fragrance, without losing effectiveness.\n\n2. Even natural ingredients can cause and trigger existing allergies. A patch test is recommended.\n\n3. In case of any rashes or allergy, please consult a specialist.\n\n4. All images shown are for illustration purpose only, actual results may vary.\n\n5. For external use only. Store in a cool & dry place.",
            "Get the App to track your order status smoothly": "Facebook\n\nTwitter\n\nInstagram\n\nYouTube\n\nTranslation missing: en.general.social.links.email"
