            "FAQ": "What is salicylic acid face wash?\nSalicylic acid face wash is a sulphate-free cleanser that reduces active acne, controls excess oil, and soothes skin inflammation, ideal for oily and acne-prone skin.\n\nIs a salicylic acid face wash right for my skin type (oily, combination, acne-prone)?\nYes, it’s perfect for oily, combination, and acne-prone skin types, providing gentle yet effective cleansing.\n\nHow can a salicylic acid face wash help clear up acne breakouts and blackheads?\nIt unclogs pores, removes dirt and excess oil, and reduces inflammation, helping to clear up acne breakouts and blackheads.\n\nWhat other benefits can I expect from a salicylic acid face wash?\nBesides treating acne, it controls oil, soothes inflammation, and leaves your skin feeling fresh and clean without drying it out.\n\nHow often should I use a salicylic acid face wash?\nUse it twice daily, morning and night, for best results.\n\nCan I use other acne treatments with a salicylic acid face wash?\nYes, but introduce them gradually to avoid irritation. Follow with toner, serum, and moisturizer.\n\nIs it okay to use a salicylic acid face wash around my eyes?\nAvoid the eye area, as the skin there is delicate and more prone to irritation.\n\nCan salicylic acid face wash irritate my skin?\nIt’s generally gentle, but if irritation occurs, reduce usage to once a day or every other day.\n\nHow long will it take to see results from using this face wash?\nYou may see improvements within a few days, with more significant results after consistent use for a few weeks.\n\nDoes salicylic acid increase sun sensitivity?\nYes, it can, so always follow with sunscreen in the morning to protect your skin.",
